{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/37166-shangri-la-and-other-places-of-power","id":37166,"title":"Shangri La and other places of power ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-25T22:28:16-08:00","id":37166,"title":"Shangri La and other places of power ?","content":"What happend with the seven shangri la, atlantis, the bermuda triangle , El Dorado , Lemuria , Castle Houska and the Garden of eden and the tower of babylonia in the OWoD cannon. are this places still reachable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T23:14:05-08:00","id":37187,"title":"","content":"They're not canon, so its up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T09:34:08-08:00","id":37373,"title":"","content":"The Garden of Eden is the only one that comes up in 'canon' as far as I know, but when I say that, it ought to be seen as an 'according-to-one-myth' sort of thing...<br /> <br /> <i>Revelations of the Dark Mother</i> for <b>Vampire: the Masqueraded</b> has information about Eden as Jehovah's Garden, saying that Lilith (Adam's first wife) made sure that Adam and Eve were booted from that paradise, and then she seduced Lucifer, who'd been tasked with guarding the gates. We're told that Jehovah shut his garden from the rest of the Creation and the from the gardens of the other Elohim after this occurred.<br /> <br /> ...Thing is, <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> has it's own version of Lucifer, and he is not at all associated with Lilith as far as I found. In fact, <i>Days of Fire</i> mentions vampires and mages and werewolves, but it very carefully does NOT mention Lilith. So it really comes down to whatever you want in your chronicle.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Atlantis is obliquely mentioned in <b>Dark Ages: Mage</b>, but it's not specifically stated as being THE Atlantis. I think there's something, somewhere about the Tower of Babel in some book, and maybe you'll find something about the Bermuda Triangle in <i>Blood Dimmed Tides</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T10:40:10-08:00","id":37395,"title":"","content":"<b>El Dorado</b> was in <b>Rage Across the Amazon</b>. And even then, it's a mini Umbral Realm, if I remember correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T12:13:45-08:00","id":37439,"title":"","content":"I'm personally more interested about the lost continents of Hiva and Lemuria since are they both located at the pacific but in general a source book of lost or mythical continents, cities etc. in WoD would be fun.<br /> <br /> But since we're bereft of such book, the internet is the next good source of cryptogeography. Just Google the names and you should find plenty of stuff to mine for your campaigns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T17:12:47-08:00","id":37569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/37166-shangri-la-and-other-places-of-power?p=37187#post37187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not canon, so its up to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually as mentioned El Dorado was a city made by an immortal Archmage, and the Archmage himself. He was killed by the Skinner Sam Haight, and reincarnated as a bird while Haight temporarily had access to his powers via an ancient Order of Reason Wonder the Conquistador's Sword.<br /> <br /> Eden is mentioned all the time, particularly in Vampire and Demon lore, but recently in Rage Across the World we are given information that the Caern situated in the believed spot where Adam and Eve were cast out in Ethiopia actually has a portal the Primordial Garden Guarded by an Unconquerable Spirit with Wings and a Flaming Sword. It hasn't been beaten, but it has been bartered with resulting in providing access to the Garden's Miracles which include reviving the Dead, reviving Extinct Species, and Bringing new Life Forms.<br /> <br /> I could have sworn Shangrila was mentioned before, probably in Mage.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Demon have mentioned of Babel's Tower. Demon has the Babel Project which seemed to be a Fallen attempt to bring awakening into humanity, and Werewolf has an Ancient Fetish that is a Cornerstone of the fabled tower.<br /> <br /> The Bermuda triangle was a number of things I think. Mentioned often in Wraith and Blood Dimmed Tides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T22:02:23-08:00","id":38160,"title":"","content":"Well, they each probably have several umbral reflections, however the specifics beyond that depends on where the ST wants to go with your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}